      <packagedElement xmi:type="uml:Class" xmi:id="cdif.bbr.metadata.cdifDataType.cdifDataStructureComponent.DimensionComponent" xmi:uuid="c433207a-3fd1-578d-bd7f-e945ae7363f9">
        <name>DimensionComponent</name>
        <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="cdif.bbr.metadata.cdifDataType.cdifDataStructureComponent.DimensionComponent.comment" xmi:uuid="a7deabb2-5dc2-5ac8-87d5-243d1872e532">
          <body>**CDIF**

Definition
==========

Role given to a represented variable in the context of a dimensional data structure to identify the universes associated with data points. The variable acts as a field in the compound identifier (the key structure) to disambiguate the cells in the multi-dimensional "cube".  AG: references to the variables which are the components of a compound identifier, in which each variable is a single field - an axis - in a coordinate system addressing a location in a matrix. These variables are often categorical, but also commonly include time. Unlike other Components, they may be ordered using instances of cdi:ComponentPosition.
:idDescription: "Identifier for this DimensionComponent node"
:rdfType: ``cdi:DimensionComponent``</body>
          <annotatedElement xmi:idref="cdif.bbr.metadata.cdifDataType.cdifDataStructureComponent.DimensionComponent"/>
        </ownedComment>
